\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Christ the Lord is risen again;
\par Christ hath broken every chain:
\par Hark! The angels shout for joy,
\par Singing ever more on high:
\par Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He who gave for us His life,
\par Who for us endure the strife,
\par Is our paschal Lamp to-day;
\par We too sing for joy, and say:
\par Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He who bore all pain and loss
\par Comfortless upon the Cross,
\par Lives in lorry know on high,
\par Pleads for us, and hears our cry:
\par Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. He whose past no records tell,
\par Who descended into hell,    
\par Who the strong man arm hath bound,
\par Now in highest heaven is crowned.
\par Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. He who slumbered in the grave
\par Is exalted now to save;
\par Now through Christendom is save;
\par That the Lamp is King of kings.
\par Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Now He bids us tell abroad
\par Now the lost may be restored,
\par How penitent forgiven,
\par How we too may enter heaven:
\par Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Thou are paschal Lamp indeed,
\par Christ to-day Thy people feed;
\par Take our skins and guilt away,
\par That we all may sing aye; 
\par Hallelujah!
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

